# SmartSuite Cache System - NEVER TOUCH

## ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN
- **Never modify `src/utils/smartsuite.ts`** - This file is off-limits
- **Never modify any cache files** - These are managed by CI/CD
- **Never attempt to "fix" or "improve"** the SmartSuite fetching logic
- **Never run SmartSuite operations locally** - This is not how the system works

## CI/CD ONLY
- SmartSuite cache system is handled entirely by CI/CD pipeline
- Cache files are updated automatically by the build process
- Local modifications will break the system and be overwritten

## User Issues Protocol
- If users have SmartSuite data problems, tell them to use the SmartSuite button/interface
- Direct them to the SmartSuite dashboard to refresh data
- **Never attempt to fix SmartSuite issues by modifying code**

## System Design
- The system reads static cache files that are updated by CI/CD
- Simple file reading approach is intentional and correct
- No HTTP fetching, no environment detection, no complex logic needed

## SmartSuite Data Fetching Rules
- **ALWAYS fetch SmartSuite data at BUILD TIME ONLY**
- Use `export const prerender = true;` in Astro pages that need SmartSuite data
- Fetch data in Astro frontmatter using `await fetchReportRecords(reportID)`
- Pass data to client-side scripts as static variables
- **NEVER fetch SmartSuite data at runtime in the browser**
- **NEVER use fetch() or HTTP requests for SmartSuite data**

## HANDS OFF POLICY
- Leave the SmartSuite system completely alone
- It works as designed when not interfered with
- Any "improvements" will break the CI/CD integration